From: Ayoub Zaki <ayoub.zaki@embetrix.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx95: add system manager reset

Add the node used by the imx-sm-reset driver. This lets Linux request a
full board reset through PSCI RESET2 with the board_reset argument.
ROM can then select the boot image set again after a firmware update.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Ayoub Zaki <ayoub.zaki@embetrix.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95.dtsi | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95.dtsi
@@ -47,6 +47,10 @@
 		serial7 = &lpuart8;
 	};
 
+	reset_ctrl {
+		compatible = "nxp,imx95-resetctrl";
+	};
+
 	cpus {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <0>;
